2. COMMERCIAL LICENCE GRANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

   Upon payment in full for a Product, the Licensor grants You a perpetual,
   worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable licence to:

   a. install and run an unlimited number of instances of that Product on
      hardware owned, leased, or otherwise controlled by You; and

   b. use that Product for Your own internal business purposes, including the
      development of Your own products.

   This grant applies separately to each Product You license.

   This is an organisation-wide (site) licence. You do not need to count
   servers, seats, CPUs, GPUs, or users.

2.1 UPDATES ARE INCLUDED, PERPETUALLY

   Every Update to a Product You have licensed is included at no further charge,
   for as long as the Licensor publishes Updates for it. There is no maintenance
   period, no renewal, and no version boundary at which Your licence stops: a
   licence to a Product covers that Product and all of its future releases.

   Your rights are not affected by the Licensor ceasing to publish Updates, by
   the price changing, or by the Product being withdrawn from sale. What You
   licensed keeps running, and whatever Updates were published remain Yours to
   download and use.

2.2 MODULES ARE SEPARATE PRODUCTS

   The Base Product does not include Modules. Each Module is licensed by a
   separate purchase, on the terms of this Agreement, and carries its own
   perpetual right to Updates under Section 2.1.

   A Module requires a licensed Base Product to run. Licensing a Module does not
   license the Base Product, and licensing the Base Product does not license any
   Module.

   A MODULE NEVER TAKES AWAY WHAT YOU ALREADY LICENSED. A capability present in
   a Product at the time You licensed it remains part of that Product and will
   not later be moved behind a separate purchase. Modules are additional
   capabilities offered alongside what You already have — the boundary is fixed
   when a Module is first offered for sale, not retroactively.

   Where a Module is offered without a separate price — bundled, promotional, or
   included in the Base Product — it is part of the Base Product for the
   purposes of the preceding paragraph.

2.3 EVALUATION LICENCE

   Where the Licensor makes a Product available without charge and identifies it
   as an evaluation, trial, or preview build, You may install and run it solely
   to evaluate it, and not in production or for any
   revenue-generating purpose. Sections 3 through 12 apply to evaluation use.
   The Licensor may withdraw an evaluation build at any time.

